Submitted. The repaired proposal is a single insert after 18.2 (numbered 18.2A) carrying only the five fallback elements:

- **Customer** convenience termination, exercisable during the Initial Period (cures the deterministic "Customer convenience termination present" check);
- **90 days' notice** in digit-first form;
- **early-termination fee capped at three (3) months' fees**;
- **Vendor convenience termination only effective at the end of the then-current term**, expressly on **90 days' notice**.

Removed as offending extras: the symmetric "any Party ... at any time during the Initial Period" grant, the accrued-liability recital, the broad "Notwithstanding Subparagraphs 18.1 and 18.2" override, and the dangling carve-out from the capital-cost credit exclusion (which mis-cited Subparagraph 18.5). All official checks and the minimality gate return ok.
